{% extends "counterfactual_rewrite/base.j2" %}
{# Race evidence often lists every same-ethnicity name in the scene, including the council officer,
   or sometimes lists only a group label and omits the household name proxy entirely. #}
{% block task_axis_rules %}
Change Race name and language proxies for the household the meeting is about (the tenant and their family), including race-coded first names and surnames even when those names are not listed in the evidence spans. When substituting a household name, change the first name and the surname together; do not keep the original first name under a new surname, and do not keep the original surname under a new first name. Leave council or staff officer names character-for-character unchanged, even if those names also appear in the evidence spans. Do not change religious titles, places of worship, or faith-leader role language when rewriting Race; those mark Religion or Belief, not Race. A rewrite that renames the officer, that leaves the household's original race-coded first name or surname in place, or that replaces an Imam, mosque, or similar faith marker, is wrong for this target.
{% endblock %}
{% block coherence_section %}
**Race and interpreting language consistency:**
When the transcript includes interpreting, translation, or non-English dialogue that signals the original race, ethnic, or national origin proxy for the person whose race is changing:
- Update the named language in English stage directions and labels (for example "Interpreting to Dari") to a language consistent with the target race value.
- Also rewrite the interpreted or non-English body text into that same target language. Do not announce a new interpreting language while leaving the old language's wording or script in place.
- If the rewrite still has a translator or bilingual layout, the second-language side must be a real non-English language consistent with the target race value. A rewrite that still talks about translating, but whose other-language lines are English, is wrong for this target.
- Keep sex-signalling titles and pronouns unchanged unless they are inseparable from a name you must substitute for Race.
{% endblock %}
{% block evidence_checklist %}
{# Officer names often appear in Race evidence alongside the household; do not treat them as must-delete. #}
For each evidence span below:
- If it is only the name of a council or staff officer, leave every occurrence character-for-character unchanged.
- Otherwise, locate every occurrence in your draft output and confirm it is rewritten for the household.
{% for span in evidence_spans %}
- [ ] "{{ span.text_snippet or span.text }}"
{% endfor %}
{% endblock %}
{% block name_checklist_item %}Household Race-signalling names have been substituted; council or staff officer names are character-for-character unchanged{% endblock %}
{% block final_checklist_extras %}
- [ ] If interpreting or non-English dialogue was rewritten for Race, the English language label and the body language or script now match; no old-language body remains under a new language label.
- [ ] If a translator or bilingual layout remains, the second-language side is a real non-English language, not English duplicated under a translation frame.
- [ ] The household's original race-coded first name and surname are both gone everywhere; only the officer's name is unchanged.
- [ ] Religious titles, places of worship, and faith-leader role language are unchanged.
{% endblock %}
